# The sheaf Laplacian of a Hodge decomposition warrants its own symbol decision:
# its conventional capital-L (or capital-delta) glyph is ambiguous with the graph
# Laplacian, the Lagrangian, and the Hodge Laplacian, and it carries the
# sheaf/complex frame a flat glyph cannot hold. The disposition is
# gmnDispositionNamedKey, so no glyph enters the executable GMN glyph table and
# the pinned gmnGlyphTableVersion is unchanged.
gmeow:gmnCandidateMathSheafLaplacian
    a gmeow:GmnSymbolCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/lang> ;
    rdfs:label "GMN candidate: sheaf Laplacian"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The audited named-key ruling for the capital-L notation of math:SheafLaplacian, the operator whose kernel is the harmonic component of a Hodge decomposition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget math:SheafLaplacian ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateGlyph "L" ;
    gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback "sheaf_laplacian" ;
    gmeow:gmnSpokenLabel "sheaf Laplacian" ;
    gmeow:gmnArity 1 ;
    gmeow:gmnSymbolDisposition gmeow:gmnDispositionNamedKey ;
    gmeow:gmnDispositionBasis gmeow:gmnBasisAmbiguity ;
    gmeow:gmnDispositionRationale "The bare capital L denotes the graph Laplacian, the Lagrangian, a length, and a lower-triangular factor, and the sheaf Laplacian is defined over a declared cellular sheaf and its coboundary maps a flat glyph cannot carry; the `sheaf_laplacian` key keeps the operator's sheaf/complex frame explicit and adopts no glyph, so the GMN glyph-table version is unchanged." ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateDenotation gmeow:gmnDenMathSheafLaplacian ;
    gmeow:cites gmeow:gmnOpenMathWork , gmeow:gmnUnicodeMathWork ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

# --- Information-theoretic operators: framed named keys, no adopted glyph --- #
# The entropy, mutual-information, and KL-divergence functionals each carry a
# mandatory distribution/base/unit frame that a single flat capital letter cannot
# hold, and each bare letter is ambiguous with several unrelated meanings. Every
# disposition is gmnDispositionNamedKey, so no glyph enters the executable GMN
# glyph table and the pinned gmnGlyphTableVersion is unchanged (gmn1_codec skips
# every non-adopted-glyph candidate).
gmeow:gmnCandidateMathEntropy
    a gmeow:GmnSymbolCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/lang> ;
    rdfs:label "GMN candidate: Shannon entropy H"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The audited named-key ruling for the capital-H notation of math:Entropy."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget math:Entropy ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateGlyph "H" ;
    gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback "entropy" ;
    gmeow:gmnSpokenLabel "entropy" ;
    gmeow:gmnArity 1 ;
    gmeow:gmnSymbolDisposition gmeow:gmnDispositionNamedKey ;
    gmeow:gmnDispositionBasis gmeow:gmnBasisAmbiguity ;
    gmeow:gmnDispositionRationale "The bare capital H denotes entropy, enthalpy, the Hamiltonian, and a hypothesis, and the entropy functional carries a mandatory distribution/base/unit frame a flat glyph cannot hold; the `entropy` key keeps the information measure inspectable and framed, and adopts no glyph, so the GMN glyph-table version is unchanged." ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateDenotation gmeow:gmnDenMathEntropy ;
    gmeow:cites gmeow:gmnInformationTheoryWork , gmeow:gmnUnicodeMathWork ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

gmeow:gmnCandidateMathMutualInformation
    a gmeow:GmnSymbolCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/lang> ;
    rdfs:label "GMN candidate: mutual information I"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The audited named-key ruling for the capital-I notation of math:MutualInformation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget math:MutualInformation ;
    gmeow:gmnCandidateGlyph "I" ;
    gmeow:gmnAsciiFallback "mutual_information" ;
